{"type":"text","text":"Done — both routines are mapped and promoted.\n\n## Routine 1 — the coin award: entry `$BBFE` (“AddCoin”)\n\nFound from the mapping's coin digits `$07ED/$07EE`. PRG contains **no** instruction with `$07ED` or `$07EE` as an operand, so the digit update had to be indirect; searching for callers led to `JSR $BBFE` at **`$BB7D`** (the block-coin spawn) and `JMP $BBFE` at **`$DE0B`** (free-coin collect routine `$DE03`).\n\nCode (`$BBFE`–`$BC48`, 75 bytes):\n\n```\n$BBFE: A9 01     lda #$01\n$BC00: 8D 39 01  sta $0139   ; BCD operand ones digit = 1\n$BC03: AE 53 07  ldx $0753\n$BC06: BC F8 BB  ldy $BBF8,x ; X=0 -> Y=$17\n$BC09: 20 5F 8F  jsr $8F5F   ; <-- adds 1 to the coin digits $07E9-$07EE\n$BC0C: EE 5E 07  inc $075E   ; <-- binary coin counter\n$BC0F: AD 5E 07  lda $075E\n$BC12: C9 64     cmp #$64\n$BC14: D0 0C     bne $BC22\n$BC16: A9 00     lda #$00\n$BC18: 8D 5E 07  sta $075E   ; reset at 100\n$BC1B: EE 5A 07  inc $075A   ; 1-UP\n$BC22: A9 02     lda #$02\n$BC24: 8D 38 01  sta $0138\n$BC2D: 20 5F 8F  jsr $8F5F   ; <-- +200 score\n$BC36: 20 06 8F  jsr $8F06   ; coin sound\n```\n\n**Job instructions:** `INC $075E` (`$BC0C`) counts the coin, and the first `JSR $8F5F` (`$BC09`) increments the coin digits. **Callers:** `JSR $BBFE` at `$BB7D`; `JMP $BBFE` at `$DE0B` from routine `$DE03`. Verified live: a jump into the first 1‑1 ? block gave `$075E=1`, coin digits `[0,1]`, HUD `x01`, score `000200` (the `2` landing at `$07E1`).\n\n## Routine 2 — the shared helper: entry `$8F5F` (“AddBCD”)\n\nFound by `trace_writes` on the self-ticking timer digits `$07F8-$07FA` for 400 frames — the single writer was **PC `$8F78`** (ROM `0x0F78`), the `DEY` right after the store in this routine.\n\n```\n$8F5F: AD 70 07  lda $0770\n$8F68: BD 34 01  lda $0134,x   ; 6-byte BCD operand, MSD first, ones at $0139\n$8F6C: 79 D7 07  adc $07D7,y   ; add into counter digit at $07D7+Y\n$8F75: 99 D7 07  sta $07D7,y   ; store (the traced write)\n$8F78: 88        dey\n$8F79: CA        dex\n$8F7A: 10 EC     bpl $8F68     ; 6 digits, ones at $07D7+Y\n```\n\nIt is a signed-digit adder: `$FF` acts as −1 (borrow at `$8F87`), `≥$0A` carries at `$8F8E`, and `$8F7C-$8F86` clears the `$0133-$0139` operand.\n\n**It is genuinely shared**, because the caller's `Y` picks which counter receives the digits:\n- `$B792` — timer/hurry: `LDY #$23`, `$0139=$FF` (−1) → target `$07F5-$07FA` = the TIME digits.\n- `$BC09` / `$BC2D` — the coin routine `$BBFE`: `Y = $BBF8,X` with `X=$0753=0` → `Y=$17` → target `$07E9-$07EE`, **ones at `$07EE`** = the coin digits; second call (`$BBFA`,`Y=$0B`) adds the 200 score.\n- `$D32E` / `$D33F` — time-up bonus.\n\nSo the routine that adds the coin is **`$BBFE`**, and the routine that actually writes the coin digits is the helper **`$8F5F`** (shared with the timer and the score). Also recorded the binary counter `$075E` (0–99, 100 → 1-UP). All three entries were recorded with source “trace and disassembly” and `promote_mappings` promoted them (mapping file now has 12 addresses plus the 2 routines).\n\nNote: I could not capture a `trace_writes` hit *during the coin grab itself* — tools execute serially against the bridge and `play_input` releases A, so the ~5-frame `?`-block bump always completes before a trace can install. The helper's write PC is instead proven by the timer trace (same routine, `Y=$23`), and the coin path by the disassembly plus the live post-coin RAM reads. The emulator is left paused in 1‑1 at a post-coin state."}
